        return []
    primes = []
    for i in range(2, n):
        if all(i % j for j in range(2, int(i**0.5) + 1)):
            primes.append(i)
    return primes
```

"Top n" is a no-op — can't have more than n-1 primes below n. Returns all primes in `[2, n)`.

